### Describe the bug

When using the moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Thinking model with tool calling and --reasoning-parser kimi_k2, the model correctly identifies all required and optional parameters during the reasoning phase (<think> block), but fails to generate optional parameters in the actual tool call output. The model's reasoning content shows it intended to include the cuisine parameter, but the final tool call arguments only contain the required parameters.

Verified data flow:

- Raw generation output from model correctly includes all three parameters in the reasoning content
- Text is properly passed through reasoning parser (separates <think> content from tool calls)
- Tool call text reaching KimiK2Detector is intact and correct
- Parser successfully extracts the two parameters that were generated
- **The problem occurs during token generation, not during parsing**


### Reproduction

```
python -m sglang.launch_server \
    --model-path moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Thinking \
    --revision 357b94aee9d50ec88e5e6dd9550fd7f957cb1baa \
    --port 12345 \
    --host 0.0.0.0 \
    --tensor-parallel-size 8 \
    --sampling-backend pytorch \
    --trust-remote-code \
    --cuda-graph-max-bs 64 \
    --enable-metrics \
    --context-length 262144 \
    --reasoning-parser kimi_k2 \
    --tool-call-parser kimi_k2
```


```
curl -X POST http://localhost:12345/v1/chat/completions \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{
  "model": "moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Thinking",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I want a seafood restaurant in Seattle that can accommodate a group of 5."
    }
  ],
  "tools": [
    {
      "type": "function",
      "function": {
        "name": "restaurant.find_group",
        "description": "Find restaurants suitable for groups based on specified criteria such as location and cuisine.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "location": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The city and state, e.g. Seattle, WA"
            },
            "cuisine": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": ["Seafood", "Italian", "Indian", "Chinese"]
              },
              "description": "Preferred cuisine at the restaurant. Default empty array"
            },
            "group_size": {
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "Size of the group that the restaurant should accommodate."
            }
          },
          "required": ["location", "group_size"]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "tool_choice": "auto",
  "separate_reasoning": true
}'
```


Expected:
```
{
  "function": {
    "name": "restaurant.find_group",
    "arguments": "{\"location\":\"Seattle, WA\",\"group_size\":5,\"cuisine\":[\"Seafood\"]}"
  }
}
```


Actual Behavior
```
{
  "reasoning_content": "...The parameters are:\n- location: \"Seattle, WA\"\n- group_size: 5\n- cuisine: [\"Seafood\"] (this is an array based on the enum)\n\nAll required parameters are provided...",
  "tool_calls": [
    {
      "function": {
        "name": "restaurant.find_group",
        "arguments": "{\"location\":\"Seattle, WA\",\"group_size\":5}"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Note: The reasoning_content clearly shows the model intended to include cuisine: ["Seafood"], but this parameter is absent from the actual tool call.


