### Motivation

## Overview

Design for adding structural tag support to Rust router, mirroring the Python architecture where each parser knows how to build its own structural tag.

**References**:
- XGrammar Structural Tag Tutorial: https://xgrammar.mlc.ai/docs/tutorials/structural_tag.html
- #13026 

---

## Table of Contents

1. [Architecture Design](#architecture-design)
2. [API Changes](#api-changes)
3. [Regular Router Changes](#regular-router-changes)
4. [Harmony Router Changes](#harmony-router-changes)

---

## Architecture Design

### Current Python Architecture

```
FunctionCallParser
  ├─ detector: BaseFormatDetector (Llama32Detector, MistralDetector, etc.)
  │   └─ build_structural_tag() → Dict[str, Any]
  └─ get_structure_constraint()
      ├─ auto mode → detector.build_structural_tag()
      └─ required mode → get_json_schema_constraint()
```

### Current Rust Architecture (Before Changes)

```
utils::generate_tool_constraints(tools, tool_choice, model)
  ├─ No connection to tool parsers
  └─ Returns json_schema for required only
```

**Problem**:
- Tool parsers exist but aren't used for constraint generation
- Format knowledge duplicated (parsers know format for parsing, utils knows format for constraints)
- No structural tag support

### Proposed Rust Architecture (After Changes)

```
Module Structure:
tool_parser/
  ├─ mod.rs (exports constraints module)
  ├─ traits.rs (ToolParser trait with build_structural_tag)
  ├─ factory.rs (ToolParserFactory - already exists)
  ├─ constraints.rs (NEW - all constraint generation logic)
  └─ parsers/
      ├─ llama_parser.rs (implements get_format_info)
      ├─ mistral_parser.rs (implements get_format_info)
      ├─ qwen_parser.rs (implements get_format_info)
      ├─ deepseek_parser.rs (overrides build_structural_tag for wrapper format)
      └─ ...

Constraint Generation Flow:
tool_parser/constraints::build_tool_call_constraint(...)
  ├─ Get parser using same pattern as get_tool_parser():
  │   ├─ If configured_parser is Some → factory.get_by_name(configured_parser)
  │   └─ Otherwise → factory.create_for_model(model)
  │
  └─ Match tool_choice:
      ├─ Auto → parser.build_structural_tag(tools, at_least_one=false, stop_after_first=!parallel)
      └─ Required/Specific → build_json_schema_constraint(tools, tool_choice, parallel_tool_calls)

ToolParser Trait (in tool_parser/traits.rs):
  ├─ get_format_info(&self, tool_name) → (begin, end, trigger)  // Per-tool format
  └─ build_structural_tag(&self, tools, at_least_one, stop_after_first) → Result<String, String>
      ├─ Default implementation: Uses get_format_info() to build triggered_tags
      └─ DeepSeek overrides: Builds wrapper + tags_with_separator format

Router Integration:
Regular: preparation.rs → constraints::build_tool_call_constraint(...)
  Passes: factory, configured_parser, model
Harmony: preparation.rs → build_tool_call_structural_tag(...)  [No changes - uses own format]
```

---

## API Changes

### 1. Add Method to ToolParser Trait

**File**: `sgl-router/src/tool_parser/traits.rs`

```rust
use serde_json::Value;

pub trait ToolParser: Send + Sync {
    // Existing methods...
    async fn parse_complete(&self, text: &str) -> ToolParserResult<(String, Vec<ToolCall>)>;
    async fn parse_incremental(&self, chunk: &str, state: &mut ParseState) -> ToolParserResult<StreamResult>;
    fn detect_format(&self, text: &str) -> bool;

    // NEW METHOD
    /// Build xgrammar structural tag for this parser's format.
    ///
    /// Args:
    ///     tools: List of available tools
    ///     at_least_one: Require at least one tool call (for tool_choice="required")
    ///     stop_after_first: Stop after first tool call (for parallel_tool_calls=false)
    ///
    /// Returns:
    ///     JSON string of structural tag in xgrammar format
    ///
    /// Default implementation returns triggered_tags format using parser-specific
    /// begin/end/trigger patterns.
    fn build_structural_tag(
        &self,
        tools: &[Tool],
        at_least_one: bool,
        stop_after_first: bool,
    ) -> Result<String, String> {
        // Default implementation for triggered_tags format
        let mut tags = Vec::new();
        let mut triggers = std::collections::HashSet::new();

        for tool in tools {
            let name = &tool.function.name;

            // Get parser-specific format info
            let (begin, end, trigger) = self.get_format_info(name);

            // Always include schema
            let schema = tool.function.parameters.clone();

            tags.push(json!({
                "format": "tag",
                "begin": begin,
                "content": {
                    "format": "json_schema",
                    "schema": schema
                },
                "end": end
            }));

            triggers.insert(trigger);
        }

        let structural_tag = json!({
            "format": "triggered_tags",
            "triggers": triggers.into_iter().collect::<Vec<_>>(),
            "tags": tags,
            "at_least_one": at_least_one,
            "stop_after_first": stop_after_first
        });

        serde_json::to_string(&structural_tag)
            .map_err(|e| format!("Failed to serialize structural tag: {}", e))
    }

    /// Get format-specific begin/end/trigger patterns for a tool.
    ///
    /// Returns: (begin, end, trigger)
    ///
    /// This method must be implemented by each parser to provide model-specific formats.
    fn get_format_info(&self, tool_name: &str) -> (String, String, String);
}
```

