### Describe the bug

Using the GRPC Router routing to a worker running gpt-oss-120b: If we send a request to the router responses API that prompts a function call, but also provide an MCP server tool, the router fails to find the function and instead tries to incorrectly invoke the function on the mcp server. I confirmed that this behavior is not seen in the openai api, so this is a bug. 

### Reproduction

Router and worker startup commands on 2xH100 host:
```
# Worker startup
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=5,6 python -m sglang.launch_server \
    --model /raid/models/openai/gpt-oss-120b \
    --port 20000 \
    --log-level debug \
    --tp-size 2 \
    --grpc-mode \


# Router startup
python -m sglang_router.launch_router \
  --worker-urls grpc://127.0.0.1:20000 \
  --model /raid/models/openai/gpt-oss-120b \
  --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8082
```

I send the following two curl commands to openai's api and the router (running locally with gpt-oss-120b) respectively. Both requests use the same prompt in which they ask for the weather, which causes the model to attempt to invoke the supplied get_weather function. An mcp server is also supplied but is not intended to be used by this prompt.

